In article <B8xO2md.rchason@delphi.com>,  <rchason@delphi.com> wrote:
>It may be nice, in future versions of Nethack, to allow the player to freely
>select an alignment, e.g. to play a chaotic Valkyrie or a neutral Knight.
>
>I suggest this mainly because Nethack equates lawful with good and chaotic
>with evil, and the idea of an evil Elf grates on me.  I know the game is
>called Nethack, and not The Silmarillion, but J.R.R. Tolkien must be turning
>in his grave at the thought of evil Elves!  I'd like to play a neutral Elf,
>without having to tick off my god and find a neutral altar.

I agree.  Elves shouldn't be classified as chaotic, anyway.  Perhaps if
the Dev Team is just rying to keep the alignments balanced, Barbarians
should be moved to chaotic, and elves to neutral.  But it would be cool to
be able to pick an alignment at the start.  I'd think most classes could
pick from all three, but some would have restrictions.  Knights, for instance,
could be lawful or chaotic (the black knight), but not neutral.  Rogues
couldn't be lawful.  Valkyries probably shouldn't be lawful either.  
Samurai should probably have to be lawful.  Any other limitations?

